WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.738
<v Examiner>Using a Punnett square.

2
00:00:02.738 --> 00:00:03.373
<v Examiner>Four marks.

3
00:00:03.823 --> 00:00:07.400
<v Examiner>Explain how a Punnett square is used to predict offspring.

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.089
<v Examiner>Work a cross of big B little b with big B little b, where brown eyes, big B,

5
00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:14.124
<v Examiner>are dominant over blue, little b.

6
00:00:14.124 --> 00:00:19.183
<v Examiner>Then work a codominant blood group cross: I A little i, crossed with I B little i.

7
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:24.042
Genetics problems are the biggest pile of marks in her Module 3 quizzes,

8
00:00:24.042 --> 00:00:26.737
and this is the tool for nearly all of them.

9
00:00:27.187 --> 00:00:30.608
The hook: one parent across the top, one down the side,

10
00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:33.096
and one letter from each into every box.

11
00:00:33.546 --> 00:00:34.434
What it shows.

12
00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.796
Genes come in pairs of alleles, one from each parent.

13
00:00:37.796 --> 00:00:42.807
A Punnett square shows all the possible combinations of the parents' alleles at

14
00:00:42.807 --> 00:00:47.882
fertilisation, so it predicts the probability of each genotype in the offspring.

15
00:00:48.332 --> 00:00:49.247
How to draw it.

16
00:00:49.247 --> 00:00:51.870
One parent's two alleles go across the top.

17
00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.798
The other parent's two alleles go down the side.

18
00:00:54.798 --> 00:00:59.617
Fill each of the four boxes with one allele from the top and one from the side.

19
00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:04.491
Cross one: big B little b, crossed with big B little b.

20
00:01:04.491 --> 00:01:09.096
The boxes: one big B big B, two big B little b, and one little b little b.

21
00:01:09.096 --> 00:01:10.217
One to two to one.

22
00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:14.200
As percentages, that's twenty-five per cent homozygous dominant,

23
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.868
fifty per cent heterozygous, and twenty-five per cent homozygous recessive.

24
00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:19.989
Now the phenotype.

25
00:01:19.989 --> 00:01:23.723
Big B big B and big B little b both show the dominant trait,

26
00:01:23.723 --> 00:01:27.644
so it's seventy-five per cent brown, twenty-five per cent blue.

27
00:01:27.644 --> 00:01:29.761
Only little b little b shows blue.

28
00:01:30.211 --> 00:01:31.888
Cross two, the blood groups.

29
00:01:31.888 --> 00:01:37.100
This is codominance: I A and I B are both expressed, and little i, which gives group O,

30
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:37.878
is recessive.

31
00:01:37.878 --> 00:01:40.275
I A little i, crossed with I B little i.

32
00:01:40.275 --> 00:01:42.910
The four boxes: I A I B, which is group A B.

33
00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.228
I A little i, group A.

34
00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:45.546
I B little i, group B.

35
00:01:45.546 --> 00:01:47.403
And little i little i, group O.

36
00:01:47.403 --> 00:01:48.961
Twenty-five per cent each.

37
00:01:48.961 --> 00:01:52.675
That's how four children can have four different blood groups.

38
00:01:54.125 --> 00:01:54.809
The traps.

39
00:01:54.809 --> 00:01:56.453
Genotype is the letters.

40
00:01:56.453 --> 00:02:00.493
Phenotype is what shows: brown or blue, or the blood group.

41
00:02:00.493 --> 00:02:02.821
When she asks for both, give both.

42
00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:08.231
Second: each box is a probability for each child, not a count of real children.

43
00:02:08.231 --> 00:02:13.161
Third, the words: heterozygous is two different letters, big B little b.

44
00:02:13.161 --> 00:02:15.010
Homozygous is two the same.

45
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.005
<v Examiner>Once more.

46
00:02:16.005 --> 00:02:18.020
<v Examiner>The Punnett square, and both crosses.

47
00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:23.241
Alleles come in pairs, one from each parent,

48
00:02:23.241 --> 00:02:28.532
and the Punnett square shows every possible combination, so the probability of each.

49
00:02:28.532 --> 00:02:31.744
One parent across the top, the other down the side.

50
00:02:31.744 --> 00:02:35.965
Big B little b crossed with big B little b gives one to two to one:

51
00:02:35.965 --> 00:02:39.807
twenty-five per cent homozygous dominant, fifty heterozygous,

52
00:02:39.807 --> 00:02:41.885
twenty-five homozygous recessive.

53
00:02:41.885 --> 00:02:44.972
So seventy-five per cent brown, twenty-five blue.

54
00:02:44.972 --> 00:02:47.932
In codominance, I A and I B are both expressed:

55
00:02:47.932 --> 00:02:53.286
I A little i crossed with I B little i gives group A B, group A, group B and group O,

56
00:02:53.286 --> 00:02:54.923
twenty-five per cent each.
